              }
            ],
            "abstract": "This essay examines the turn towards science fiction and science fictional tropes in contemporary art as a way of providing a generic frame to process the climate crisis through forms of relational and intersectional aesthetics. The first half of the essay aims to establish how science fiction has become an increasingly significant set of tropes and tactics in the practice and curation of art in the twenty-first century. The second half particularly examines contemporary artists, works and movements associated with Afrofuturism, the Black fantastic, Gulf Futurism, and Arabfuturism and ends with the 2024 exhibition in Paris, Arabofuturs, as one culmination of these trends privileging SF and the SFnal as a mode of contemporary art practice that can effectively address the climate crisis",
